ekyc-service
============

Reads a Vietnamese Citizen ID card (CCCD) - printed MRZ, live face scan,
and the card's embedded NFC chip - extracts identity/biometric data, and
stores it keyed by user_id (validated against user-service). Hexagonal
architecture wired with go.uber.org/fx - see internal/domain/port for the
ports every adapter under internal/adapter implements. Static files (card
photos, chip portraits, face-scan crops) live in MinIO (chart/minio);
Postgres holds only their object keys, plus the extracted fields.

Card/face algorithms - two selectable providers behind the same
CardReader/FaceAnalyzer ports (CARD_READER_PROVIDER / FACE_ANALYZER_PROVIDER
env vars, default "native"):
  - native (default): in-house, no external runtime deps. Otsu
    binarization + fixed-pitch glyph template-matching OCR over the MRZ,
    checksum-validated per ICAO 9303 TD1 (internal/adapter/secondary/
    cardreader); pigo (pure-Go) face detection + a Local Binary Pattern
    histogram template, chi-square matched, Laplacian-variance quality
    gating (internal/adapter/secondary/facebio). Classical CV, not deep
    learning - accuracy depends on a well-lit, aligned capture (the same
    assumption real eKYC capture UIs enforce client-side).
  - python: heavier, higher-accuracy. EasyOCR (deep-learning OCR) for card
    text, face_recognition's dlib ResNet 128-d embeddings for face
    biometrics, invoked via subprocess (internal/adapter/secondary/
    pyextract, python/extract_id.py). Needs the python Docker image
    variant (~1-2GB, see Dockerfile) and PYTHON_BIN/PYTHON_EXTRACT_SCRIPT/
    PYTHON_TIMEOUT configured.

NFC chip reading (internal/adapter/secondary/nfcreader): the physical RF
handshake (ISO 14443 + APDU + Basic Access Control) can only happen on a
device with an NFC radio - a phone - never over the network from this
backend, so this decodes+verifies a chip dump a client already extracted:
BER-TLV parsing of EF.COM/DG1/DG2/EF.SOD, MRZ from DG1 (reusing the same
domain/mrz TD1 parser/checksum logic as the OCR path), the portrait from
DG2, and each data group's hash checked against EF.SOD's CMS-signed hash
list (go.mozilla.org/pkcs7). EF.SOD's signature is checked for internal
self-consistency only (content + embedded Document Signer Certificate +
signature all agree) - NOT a full CSCA trust-chain validation, which would
need that country's root certificate store, not available here. A BAC
key-derivation function (ICAO 9303 Appendix D) is included as a standalone,
independently-testable primitive for a client that wants it; there's no
live secure-messaging session here since there's no chip to run one
against. POST /api/v1/ekyc/:user_id/nfc-chip.

Config: env vars (config.FromEnv) or Consul KV, same convention as every
other service in this repo - see HostConsul/KeyConsul/ServiceConsul and
internal/infrastructure/config_provider.go.

API: see internal/adapter/primary/http/routes.go.
